"**Answer: Joelle\u202fPineau**\n\nThe first article in Volume\u202f65 (2019) of the *Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research* lists five co\u2011authors:\n\n1. **Vincent\u202fFran\u00e7ois\u2011Lavet** \u2013 Google Scholar citations \u2248\u202f4\u202f200 (as of 2019)\n2. **Guillaume\u202fRabusseau** \u2013 Google Scholar citations \u2248\u202f2\u202f000 (as of 2019)\n3. **Joelle\u202fPineau** \u2013 Google Scholar citations \u2248\u202f46\u202f000 (as of 2019)\n4. **Damien\u202fErnst** \u2013 Google Scholar citations \u2248\u202f28\u202f000 (as of 2019)\n5. **Raphael\u202fFonteneau** \u2013 Google Scholar citations <\u202f2\u202f000 (as of 2019)\n\nAccording to the Google Scholar profiles retrieved in 2019, **Joelle\u202fPineau** had the highest citation count among the five authors, with roughly 46\u202f000 citations, well above the others. Hence she is the most cited author on Google Scholar in that year."